cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "infrastructure-logbook: the fabric's record of itself"
abstract: >
  The conventions, doc gates, delivery ledger and logbook for a workspace of 53
  repositories. Sixteen gates, each shipped with a negative control, derive every
  documented count, name, branch and licence from the fabric manifest or from the
  live remotes and fail the build on drift. The ledger books hours from git history
  as Beancount transactions, allocated so concurrent sessions in different checkouts
  cannot be counted twice, and holds the plan in a separate commodity so an estimate
  can never read as progress; three-point estimates are quantiles of a lognormal
  posterior predictive rather than of the observed sample. Memory is stored as
  OpenUSD layers validated by the system usdcat. The logbook keeps retractions
  beside what they retract.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/infrastructure-logbook"
keywords:
  - documentation-testing
  - double-entry-accounting
  - beancount
  - openusd
  - project-estimation

references:

  # ── Tools this depends on and does not vendor ────────────────────────────────
  # Each is installed on the operating system and invoked as a subprocess. None is
  # imported or vendored, which is why a GPL-2.0 tool can gate an MIT repository:
  # running a program is not linking to it.

  - type: software
    title: "Beancount: double-entry accounting from text files"
    authors:
      - family-names: Blais
        given-names: Martin
    year: 2026
    version: 3.2.3
    license: GPL-2.0
    url: "https://github.com/beancount/beancount"
    notes: >
      bean-check validates ledger/spent.beancount and ledger/planned.beancount and
      exits non-zero on any error, which is what makes it a gate. Installed with
      brew, never vendored and never imported: GPL-2.0 is restricted under the
      third-party licence policy this project follows, and keeping it outside the
      tree is a licence decision as much as a dependency one.
  - type: software
    title: "OpenUSD: Universal Scene Description"
    authors:
      - name: "Pixar Animation Studios"
    year: 2026
    license: Apache-2.0
    url: "https://github.com/PixarAnimationStudios/OpenUSD"
    notes: >
      memory/*.usda are typed dictionaries in canonical usda. The system usdcat
      re-emits each layer and the bytes must match, which is what keeps a
      hand-written emitter honest. Nothing here imports pxr, for the reason
      openusd-fabric's codeless schemas already record: the ABI trap between
      Blender's, Unity's and idtx-flow's bundled builds.

  # ── Designs this implements ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - type: article
    title: >
      Holographic Reduced Representations: Distributed Representation for
      Cognitive Structures
    authors:
      - family-names: Plate
        given-names: "Tony A."
    year: 1995
    journal: "IEEE Transactions on Neural Networks"
    volume: 6
    issue: 3
    start: 623
    end: 641
    doi: "10.1109/72.377968"
    notes: >
      misc/scripts/hrr.py binds and bundles memory vectors by circular
      convolution over a uint16 phase grid, so recall is nearest neighbour over
      meaning rather than substring match. Byte-identical to tw_hrr.hpp.
  - type: report
    title: "The 'Average Man'?"
    authors:
      - family-names: Daniels
        given-names: "Gilbert S."
    year: 1952
    institution:
      name: "Wright Air Development Center, USAF"
    number: "WCRD 53-7"
    notes: >
      Of 4,063 pilots measured on ten dimensions, none was average on all ten, and
      the fix was an adjustable cockpit rather than a better mean. The delivery
      budget is fixed at one week and the scope slides for the same reason: the
      same five tasks cost 13.81 h at the median and 51.24 h at the 99th
      percentile, so no single scope fits both.
  - type: report
    title: >
      Program Evaluation Research Task, Summary Report, Phase 1
    authors:
      - name: "Special Projects Office, Bureau of Naval Weapons, U.S. Navy"
    year: 1958
    notes: >
      te = (o + 4m + p) / 6 and the critical path. ledger/planned.beancount holds
      each task's three points as metadata and misc/scripts/ledger.py computes the
      path from the dependencies, so the estimate and the picture of it cannot
      disagree. The three points are quantiles of a Bayesian posterior predictive
      rather than of the observed sample, because two of the empirical percentiles
      were single observations.

  # ── Sibling projects this manifest is the source of truth for ────────────────
  - type: software
    title: "contract-entity-packet: 100-byte entity wire-packet codec"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-entity-packet"
  - type: software
    title: "contract-patch-verify: independent Lean witness-DAG oracle for CASSIE patch detection"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/fire/contract-patch-verify"
  - type: software
    title: "interactor-triangulation: DMWT triangulation and isotropic remeshing of a closed 3D polygon"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/fire/interactor-triangulation"
  - type: software
    title: "datasource-queen: durable state, SQLite on a VFS whose pages live in FoundationDB"
    authors:
